{"name":"Fresh Air","hex":"#a6e7ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresh air","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The natural, clean air from outside, as opposed to the relatively stuffy air inside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh_air"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fresh Air (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fresh Air is a 1999 Australian film directed by Neil Mansfield and produced by Rosemary Blight, starring Marin Mimica, Nadine Garner and Bridie Carter. Set over one week in July 1998, the film tells the story of Jack, Kit and E, three housemates who live together in the Sydney suburb of Marrickville. The narrative is based on a zine within the film called Pretty Ugly made by one of the characters, and is presented non-chronologically in an editing style inspired by zine culture that Mansfield called \"zinema.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/80/Fresh_Air_1999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_Air_(film)"},{"title":"Fresh Air (Homeshake album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fresh Air is the third studio album by Canadian recording project Homeshake. It was released on February 3, 2017 through Royal Mountain Records in Canada and Sinderlyn record label in the United States. The first track off the album, \"Call Me Up\", was premiered on November 1, 2016."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/23/Homeshake_-_Fresh_Air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_Air_(Homeshake_album)"},{"title":"Fresh Air","blocks":[{"text":"Fresh Air is an American radio talk show broadcast on National Public Radio stations across the United States since 1987. It is produced by WHYY-FM in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, and hosted by Terry Gross and Tonya Mosley. The show is fed live weekdays at 12:00 noon ET, and some stations carry Fresh Air Weekend, a re-programming of highlights of the week's interviews. It won Peabody Awards in 1994 and 2022."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_Air"},{"title":"Atmosphere of Earth","blocks":[{"text":"The atmosphere of Earth consists of a layer of mixed gas that is retained by gravity, surrounding the Earth's surface. It contains variable quantities of suspended aerosols and particulates that create weather features such as clouds and hazes. The atmosphere serves as a protective buffer between the Earth's surface and outer space. It shields the surface from most meteoroids and ultraviolet solar radiation, reduces diurnal temperature variation – the temperature extremes between day and night, and keeps it warm through heat retention via the greenhouse effect. The atmosphere redistributes heat and moisture among different regions via air currents, and provides the chemical and climate conditions that allow life to exist and evolve on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/330px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atmosphere_of_Earth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Static_Electricity_2020.jpg/250px-Static_Electricity_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/60/Static_Electricity_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Static_Electricity_2020.jpg/250px-Static_Electricity_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Film poster for Static Electricity, Mansfield's recut of Fresh Air released in 2020.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStatic_Electricity_2020.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg/330px-Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg/330px-Terry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Terry Gross, host of the NPR radio program Fresh Air, in the WHYY studios in Philadelphia in 2004","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATerry_gross_fresh_air_npr_radio_host.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg/500px-Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg/1280px-Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg/500px-Fresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" R.E.M.'s Michael Stipe has been interviewed by host Terry Gross.[citation needed]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFresh_Air_with_R.E.M..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg/500px-ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg/1280px-ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg/500px-ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Afterglow of the troposphere (orange), the stratosphere (blue) and the mesosphere (dark) at which atmospheric entry begins, leaving smoke trails, such as in this case of a spacecraft reentry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Kittinger-jump.jpg/500px-Kittinger-jump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Kittinger-jump.jpg/1280px-Kittinger-jump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Kittinger-jump.jpg/500px-Kittinger-jump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In 1960, Joseph Kittinger set a record by parachuting from a gondola at 31.3 km (19.4 mi)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKittinger-jump.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/ISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg/500px-ISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/ISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg/1280px-ISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/ISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg/500px-ISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Earth from orbit, showing sunlight filtered into a reddish hue by the troposphere, while casting shadows from different cloud types. The stratosphere forms a thin band of blue scattered sunlight along the horizon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS-47_Islands_In_The_Sky%2C_Indonesia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum